==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}
[[Image:Goodyear Wrangler SR-A P23570R16.jpg|thumb|шина]]

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|de|Schiene}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ши́на}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-шина.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ши́на}}

# {{lb|ru|automotive}} [[tire]]/[[tyre]]
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1998|author=w:ru:Борис Акунин<t:{{w|Boris Akunin}}>|title=w:ru:[[Левиафан (роман Акунина)|Левиафан]]|chapter=Часть первая. Порт-Саид — Аден. Кларисса Стамп|location=Москва|publisher=w:ru:[[Захаров (издательство)|Захаров]]|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Andrew Bromfield|title2=w:en:[[Murder on the Leviathan|Leviathan]]|location2=London|publisher2=w:en:Weidenfeld & Nicolson|year2=2004|page2=|pageurl2=|text=Навстре́чу, шурша́ каучу́ковыми '''ши́нами''', кати́л на трёхколё́сном америка́нском велосипе́де ми́стер Фандо́рин.|t=There was Mr Fandorin riding towards her with a squeak of rubber '''tyres''' on his American tricycle.}}
# {{lb|ru|medicine}} [[splint]]
# [[bus]] (electrical conductor)

====Usage notes====
Strictly speaking, ши́на refers to an inflatable tube which contains air within itself, and which today is often called an "inner tube." This is distinguished from a {{l|ru|покры́шка}}, which today is often called a "tubeless tire" (in which air is not within the tire itself, but is retained in the space between the tire and the rim by an airtight seal). However, outside of mechanical circles, the words ши́на and покры́шка are often used interchangeably. 

